Fundamentals of single-particle transport — Kulkarni, Baron and Willeke (@cm-single-particle-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cm-sources) { r_34AB62TA1PZDEMM8QQZ0W3A06B
Pramod Kulkarni, Paul A. Baron and Klaus Willeke. *Fundamentals of Single Particle Transport*, chapter 2 of *Aerosol Measurement: Principles, Techniques, and Applications*, third edition, 2011, pages 15–30. [CDC Stacks record](https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/192970) · [Sixteen-page chapter](https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/192970/cdc_192970_DS1.pdf).

Read the whole chapter alongside the university notes: fluid and particle scales, drag, mobility, diffusion, gravity/inertia, electrical forces and other migration mechanisms. Section 2.6.3 treats thermal, optical, acoustic and concentration-gradient effects; follow its original references for a quantitative specialist model.

The catalogue and browser-exposed PDF title, contents and introduction were inspected on 30 October 2026. Local retrieval returned 403 and later web retrieval timed out; detailed equations and figures have not been independently checked. The PDF author order differs from the catalogue. Stacks labels the item Public Domain, while the PDF includes a Wiley copyright notice and a nonfederal contributor. Preserve both notices and component credits; do not infer unrestricted reuse of the whole chapter. The document remains an external reading, not copied content.

